Software Architecture Overview

Architectural diagram of all major components

``` text
[ Mobile App / Web App ]             [ Employee Interface ]
         |                                      |
         +--------------- HTTPS / REST --------+
                            |
                  [ API Gateway / Router ]
                            |
             +--------------+--------------+
             |              |              |
          [Auth]          [Fleet]       [Rentals]
             |              |              |
             +--------------+--------------+
                            |
                    [ Data Access Layer ]
                            |
                [ PostgreSQL Database ]
                            |
                [ Encrypted PDF Storage ]
```

Architecture explanation: The mobile app, web app, and employee
interface send requests to the API Gateway using HTTPS and REST. The API
Gateway routes requests to the correct backend service. Auth manages
account sign-in and authentication, Fleet manages vehicle records and
availability, and Rentals manages reservations and rental contracts.
These services use the data access layer to read and update information
in the PostgreSQL database. Signed rental PDFs are kept in encrypted
document storage, while the database stores the related reservation and
document references. Passwords are stored as hashes, and payment details
are represented by a payment token rather than a full card number.

